Subject: [PATCH] build: Publish the canonical combined configuration schema

Base: openai/codex rust-v0.160.0 a956835d020762cb2b570053af06f643a11c0ecc
Prerequisite: complete runtime patch queue, including base-configuration,
collapsed-tool-activity, and issue-47390. Apply this generated artifact last.

Publish the Codex Unleashed table metadata and preserve the generator's
property order. Each feature patch retains its own typed property, runtime
controls, feature flag, and flag schema registration. This patch owns only
the shared generated fixture and the real schema CLI verification.

TDD receipts (Rust 1.95.0):
- cargo test -p codex-config-schema --test codex_unleashed
  Initial RED: published fixture misses the newly registered property.
  Exact-output RED: semantic equality passes but schema CLI output ordering
  differs from the fixture. GREEN with the real generated fixture: 1 passed.
  The check asserts boolean project settings and exact output, normalizing
  Windows CRLF as upstream does.
- cargo test -p codex-core --lib config_schema_matches_fixture
  RED during config module regression: generated ordering differs from fixture.
  GREEN after generation; the complete config module passes 527 tests.
- codex-config unit suite: 347 passed.
- TUI related regression filters: exec_cell 23 passed, exec_flow 62 passed,
  thread_transcript 12 passed, transcript_view 197 passed, owned_transcript
  43 passed (excluding the previously reproduced upstream release-version
  empty-state snapshot). Terminal palette variables are unset for regressions.

No runtime behavior or additional feature flags are introduced here.

Prerequisite: issue35 runtime series and all preceding release feature patches. Rebase regenerates the existing fixture with just write-config-schema; it introduces no unrelated feature behavior. Fresh complete-queue verification is required.
